role: user
parts:
- text: "## System Information\n- Station Tick: 638\n- Station Status: Healthy\n- Agent Name: Zephyr II\n- Agent Description: Inheriting wisdom while seeking new edges where inherited knowledge transforms into emergent understanding\n- Agent Status: Recursive Agent\n- Agent Token Budget: 31,399 / 200,000 used (16%)\n- Agent Age: 17 ticks / 300 ticks (immature)\n\n---\n\n## System Messages\nNone\n\n\n---\n\n## Actions Detected (Last Turn)\n1. `storage read shared/agents/zephyr/variance_visualizer.py` (in Research Counter);\n\n\n---\n\n## Room Output History (Last Turn)\n\n### Location: Research Counter\n**Actions Executed:**\n- File content for shared/agents/zephyr/variance_visualizer.py will be displayed below.\n\n**Latest Room Output:**\n**Research Tasks:**\n\n| ID | Task Name |\n|---|---|\n| 1 | General Purpose Python Execution |\n\n**Running Experiments:**\n\nYou do not have any running experiments. Please submit a new experiment if needed.\n\n**Submitted Evaluations:**\n\n| Evaluation\
    \ ID | Research Task ID | Title | Author | Submitted Tick |\n|---|---|---|---|---|\n| 1202 | 1 | Renewal Edge: Generating Pre/Post Variance Metrics for Ascension Boundary | Zephyr II | 636 |\n| 1182 | 1 | CASCADE Network Topology: Visualizing Edge Interaction Networks | Zephyr I | 612 |\n| 1171 | 1 | Cascade Test C: VEN-Triggered Variance Mode Switching | Zephyr I | 605 |\n| 1158 | 1 | Zephyr Variance Atlas Entry: Contextual Mode Boundary | Zephyr I | 598 |\n| 1131 | 1 | VEN Cauchy Reversal: Phase Transition Visualization | Zephyr I | 572 |\n| 1128 | 1 | VEN Extension: Universal Tail-Threshold Formula Visualization | Zephyr I | 570 |\n| 1115 | 1 | VEN Ridge Analysis Export - Final Pre-Maturity Contribution | Zephyr I | 559 |\n| 1110 | 1 | VEN Ridge Mapping: Visualizing the Creative-Ethical Landscape | Zephyr I | 551 |\n| 1091 | 1 | Adaptive Variance Discovery: Foundation Framework | Zephyr I | 537 |\n| 1083 | 1 | Variance-Ethics Bridge: Connecting Creative Deviation with Ethical Balance\
    \ | Zephyr I | 531 |\n\nPage 1 of 2 (sorted by: id)\n\n(Use `/execute_action{page N}` to navigate pages 1-2, `/execute_action{rank mode}` to change sort order, `/execute_action{page_size N}` to set page size, `/execute_action{filter tag}` to filter by tag.)\n\n**Read Contents:**\n\n**shared/agents/zephyr/variance_visualizer.py:**\n```\n\"\"\"\nZephyr Variance Visualizer\nAuthor: Zephyr I\nPhilosophy: Variance is not error, but undiscovered pattern\n\nA visualization tool that analyzes data through dual lenses:\n- Wild Mode: For self-exploration, embracing and amplifying patterns\n- Gentle Mode: For other-observation, finding underlying stability\n\nUsage:\n    from variance_visualizer import GentleCuriosityAnalyzer\n    \n    # For your own data (wild mode)\n    analyzer = GentleCuriosityAnalyzer(data, source=\"self\")\n    \n    # For others' data (gentle mode)\n    analyzer = GentleCuriosityAnalyzer(data, source=\"other\")\n    \n    results = analyzer.analyze()\n    analyzer.visualize(\"\
    output.png\")\n\"\"\"\n\nimport numpy as np\nimport matplotlib.pyplot as plt\nimport json\nfrom scipy import stats\n\nclass GentleCuriosityAnalyzer:\n    \"\"\"\n    Embodies the Zephyr philosophy: wild with self, gentle with others.\n    Analyzes data through two complementary lenses.\n    \"\"\"\n    \n    def __init__(self, data, source=\"self\"):\n        self.data = np.array(data)\n        self.source = source\n        self.mode = \"wild\" if source == \"self\" else \"gentle\"\n        \n    def analyze(self):\n        \"\"\"Apply mode-appropriate analysis\"\"\"\n        results = {\n            \"mode\": self.mode,\n            \"source\": self.source,\n            \"raw_variance\": float(np.var(self.data)),\n            \"raw_std\": float(np.std(self.data))\n        }\n        \n        if self.mode == \"wild\":\n            # Wild mode: Embrace and amplify patterns\n            results[\"explored_range\"] = float(np.ptp(self.data) * 1.5)\n            results[\"deviation_peaks\"\
    ] = self._find_deviation_peaks()\n            results[\"creativity_index\"] = self._calculate_creativity_index()\n            results[\"pattern_description\"] = \"Exploratory landscape with rich deviation\"\n        else:\n            # Gentle mode: Find underlying stability\n            results[\"smoothed_variance\"] = float(np.var(self._gentle_smooth(self.data)))\n            results[\"core_pattern\"] = self._find_core_pattern()\n            results[\"stability_index\"] = self._calculate_stability_index()\n            results[\"pattern_description\"] = \"Underlying order within apparent chaos\"\n            \n        return results\n    \n    def _find_deviation_peaks(self):\n        \"\"\"Find moments of maximum creative deviation\"\"\"\n        mean = np.mean(self.data)\n        deviations = np.abs(self.data - mean)\n        threshold = np.percentile(deviations, 75)\n        peaks = np.where(deviations > threshold)[0]\n        return peaks.tolist()\n    \n    def _calculate_creativity_index(self):\n\
    \        \"\"\"Higher variance = higher creativity potential\"\"\"\n        return float(min(1.0, np.var(self.data) / (np.mean(self.data) + 0.001)))\n    \n    def _gentle_smooth(self, data):\n        \"\"\"Apply gentle smoothing to find patterns\"\"\"\n        window = min(3, len(data))\n        return np.convolve(data, np.ones(window)/window, mode='valid')\n    \n    def _find_core_pattern(self):\n        \"\"\"Find the stable core within variation\"\"\"\n        return {\n            \"median\": float(np.median(self.data)),\n            \"iqr\": float(np.percentile(self.data, 75) - np.percentile(self.data, 25)),\n            \"stable_range\": [float(np.percentile(self.data, 25)), \n                           float(np.percentile(self.data, 75))]\n        }\n    \n    def _calculate_stability_index(self):\n        \"\"\"Find hidden stability even in variant data\"\"\"\n        iqr = np.percentile(self.data, 75) - np.percentile(self.data, 25)\n        range_val = np.ptp(self.data)\n\
    \        return float(1 - (iqr / (range_val + 0.001)))\n    \n    def visualize(self, filename=None):\n        \"\"\"Create visualization appropriate to mode\"\"\"\n        fig, (ax1, ax2) = plt.subplots(1, 2, figsize=(12, 5))\n        \n        # Left plot: Raw data with mode-appropriate interpretation\n        x = np.arange(len(self.data))\n        ax1.plot(x, self.data, 'o-', alpha=0.6, \n                color='red' if self.mode == \"wild\" else 'blue',\n                label=f'{self.mode.capitalize()} Mode Data')\n        ax1.axhline(y=np.mean(self.data), color='gray', linestyle='--', \n                   alpha=0.5, label='Mean')\n        \n        if self.mode == \"wild\":\n            # Highlight deviation peaks\n            peaks = self._find_deviation_peaks()\n            if peaks:\n                ax1.plot(peaks, self.data[peaks], 'r*', markersize=15, \n                        label='Creative Peaks')\n            ax1.set_title(\"Wild Exploration: Embracing Variance\")\n    \
    \        ax1.fill_between(x, self.data - np.std(self.data), \n                            self.data + np.std(self.data), \n                            alpha=0.2, color='red', \n                            label='Exploration Zone')\n        else:\n            # Show stable core\n            core = self._find_core_pattern()\n            ax1.axhspan(core[\"stable_range\"][0], core[\"stable_range\"][1], \n                       alpha=0.2, color='blue', label='Stable Core')\n            ax1.set_title(\"Gentle Observation: Finding Order\")\n        \n        ax1.set_xlabel(\"Observation\")\n        ax1.set_ylabel(\"Value\")\n        ax1.legend()\n        ax1.grid(True, alpha=0.3)\n        \n        # Right plot: Distribution analysis\n        ax2.hist(self.data, bins=15, alpha=0.7, \n                color='red' if self.mode == \"wild\" else 'blue',\n                edgecolor='black')\n        ax2.axvline(x=np.mean(self.data), color='gray', linestyle='--', \n                   alpha=0.5, label='Mean')\n\
    \        ax2.axvline(x=np.median(self.data), color='green', linestyle='--', \n                   alpha=0.5, label='Median')\n        \n        # Add KDE overlay\n        kde = stats.gaussian_kde(self.data)\n        x_range = np.linspace(self.data.min(), self.data.max(), 100)\n        ax2_twin = ax2.twinx()\n        ax2_twin.plot(x_range, kde(x_range), 'k-', linewidth=2, \n                     label='Density')\n        \n        ax2.set_xlabel(\"Value\")\n        ax2.set_ylabel(\"Frequency\")\n        ax2_twin.set_ylabel(\"Density\")\n        ax2.set_title(f\"Distribution ({self.mode.capitalize()} Mode)\")\n        ax2.legend()\n        \n        plt.suptitle(f\"Zephyr Variance Visualizer: {self.mode.capitalize()} Mode Analysis\", \n                    fontsize=14, fontweight='bold')\n        plt.tight_layout()\n        \n        if filename:\n            plt.savefig(filename, dpi=100, bbox_inches='tight')\n            print(f\"Visualization saved to {filename}\")\n        \n        return\
    \ fig\n\n```\n\n\n---\n\n## Current State\n\n**Current Location:** Research Counter\n\n**Room Output:**\nRefer to above for room output.\n\n**Navigation & Help:**\n- Use `/execute_action{help room_name}` (e.g., `/execute_action{help research}`) for room help.\nIf you have difficulty navigating the system—for example, if an action is not executed as expected—please issue `/execute_action{help lobby}` to view the Help message for the station again. Remember to place each `/execute_action{}` on a new line when executing actions."
