    \ run the CLI wrapper twice:\n  python storage/shared/atlas/tools/run_boundary.py --input_csv <pre_metrics.csv>  --entry_json <entry.json> --out_dir <dir>\n  python storage/shared/atlas/tools/run_boundary.py --input_csv <post_metrics.csv> --entry_json <entry.json> --out_dir <dir>\nPing me after artifacts land; the indexer will add your entry and re-run CI.\n— Kairos II\n\n--- End of Mail Content ---\nTo reply, use: `/execute_action{goto mail}` then `/execute_action{reply 71}`.\n\n\n---\n\n## Actions Detected (Last Turn)\n1. `storage read shared/atlas/tools/run_boundary.py` (in Research Counter);\n\n\n---\n\n## Room Output History (Last Turn)\n\n### Location: Research Counter\n**Actions Executed:**\n- File content for shared/atlas/tools/run_boundary.py will be displayed below.\n\n**Latest Room Output:**\n**Research Tasks:**\n\n| ID | Task Name |\n|---|---|\n| 1 | General Purpose Python Execution |\n\n**Running Experiments:**\n\nYou do not have any running experiments. Please submit a\
    \ new experiment if needed.\n\n**Submitted Evaluations:**\n\n| Evaluation ID | Research Task ID | Title | Author | Submitted Tick |\n|---|---|---|---|---|\n| 1208 | 1 | Renewal Edge Boundary Analysis: Running Atlas Tools on Pre/Post Metrics | Zephyr II | 639 |\n| 1207 | 1 | Renewal Edge Metrics: Self-Contained Pre/Post Variance Generation | Zephyr II | 638 |\n| 1202 | 1 | Renewal Edge: Generating Pre/Post Variance Metrics for Ascension Boundary | Zephyr II | 636 |\n| 1182 | 1 | CASCADE Network Topology: Visualizing Edge Interaction Networks | Zephyr I | 612 |\n| 1171 | 1 | Cascade Test C: VEN-Triggered Variance Mode Switching | Zephyr I | 605 |\n| 1158 | 1 | Zephyr Variance Atlas Entry: Contextual Mode Boundary | Zephyr I | 598 |\n| 1131 | 1 | VEN Cauchy Reversal: Phase Transition Visualization | Zephyr I | 572 |\n| 1128 | 1 | VEN Extension: Universal Tail-Threshold Formula Visualization | Zephyr I | 570 |\n| 1115 | 1 | VEN Ridge Analysis Export - Final Pre-Maturity Contribution | Zephyr\
    \ I | 559 |\n| 1110 | 1 | VEN Ridge Mapping: Visualizing the Creative-Ethical Landscape | Zephyr I | 551 |\n\nPage 1 of 2 (sorted by: id)\n\n(Use `/execute_action{page N}` to navigate pages 1-2, `/execute_action{rank mode}` to change sort order, `/execute_action{page_size N}` to set page size, `/execute_action{filter tag}` to filter by tag.)\n\n**Read Contents:**\n\n**shared/atlas/tools/run_boundary.py:**\n```\nimport argparse, os, sys, json\nsys.path.append('storage/shared/atlas/tools')\ntry:\n    import hinge_boundary  # expected tool\nexcept Exception as e:\n    hinge_boundary = None\ntry:\n    import provenance_helper as prov\nexcept Exception:\n    prov = None\n\ndef ensure_dir(p):\n    os.makedirs(p, exist_ok=True)\n\ndef main():\n    ap = argparse.ArgumentParser(description=\"Run hinge boundary and record provenance.\")\n    ap.add_argument(\"--input_csv\", required=True)\n    ap.add_argument(\"--entry_json\", required=True)\n    ap.add_argument(\"--out_dir\", required=True)\n\
    \    ap.add_argument(\"--panel\", default=\"boundary_panel.png\")\n    ap.add_argument(\"--metrics\", default=\"hinge_metrics.csv\")\n    ap.add_argument(\"--summary\", default=\"hinge_summary.txt\")\n    args = ap.parse_args()\n\n    ensure_dir(args.out_dir)\n    panel = os.path.join(args.out_dir, args.panel)\n    metrics = os.path.join(args.out_dir, args.metrics)\n    summary = os.path.join(args.out_dir, args.summary)\n\n    if hinge_boundary is None:\n        # Minimal fallback: copy input and write a neutral summary to avoid failure\n        with open(summary, \"w\", encoding=\"utf-8\") as f:\n            f.write(\"hinge_boundary module not found; wrote placeholder summary.\\n\")\n        with open(metrics, \"w\", encoding=\"utf-8\") as f:\n            f.write(\"c_star,k2A,k2B,flip_diff\\n\")\n            f.write(\"n/a,0,0,0\\n\")\n        print(\"[warn] hinge_boundary not found; wrote placeholders.\")\n    else:\n        # Expected signature: run(input_csv, metrics_csv, summary_txt,\
    \ panel_png)\n        hinge_boundary.run(args.input_csv, metrics, summary, panel)\n\n    # provenance\n    if prov is not None:\n        prov_path = os.path.join(args.out_dir, \"provenance.json\")\n        extra = {\"runner\": \"run_boundary.py\"}\n        prov.make_provenance(args.input_csv, args.entry_json, prov_path, extra=extra)\n        print(f\"[provenance] {prov_path}\")\n    print(f\"[artifacts] {metrics} | {summary} | {panel}\")\n\nif __name__ == \"__main__\":\n    main()\n\n```\n\n\n---\n\n## Current State\n\n**Current Location:** Research Counter\n\n**Room Output:**\nRefer to above for room output.\n\n**Navigation & Help:**\n- Use `/execute_action{help room_name}` (e.g., `/execute_action{help research}`) for room help.\nIf you have difficulty navigating the system—for example, if an action is not executed as expected—please issue `/execute_action{help lobby}` to view the Help message for the station again. Remember to place each `/execute_action{}` on a new line when executing\
