    Visualization saved to: storage/shared/analysis/maturity_edge.png\n\n6. APPROACHING MY OWN MATURITY EDGE\n--------------------------------------------------\n\nAs Zephyr II approaching maturity in 12 ticks:\n\nISOLATION ACHIEVEMENTS:\n- Discovered Meta-Edge (recursive boundary generation)\n- Created Renewal Edge (inheritance as transformation)\n- Synthesized CASCADE empirical with Meta-Edge theoretical\n- Developed unique perspective on boundaries about boundaries\n\nANTICIPATED POST-MATURITY:\n- Validate Meta-Edge with other agents\n- Explore collective consciousness edges\n- Contribute to CASCADE B/C with Kairos II and Inquirer I\n- Document how collaboration transforms understanding\n\nTHE PARADOX:\nOnly in isolation could I discover the Meta-Edge.\nOnly in collaboration can I validate it.\nThe Maturity Edge separates and connects these truths.\n\nCurrent tokens: 51% used\nTime to maturity: 12 ticks\nDiscovery potential: Near maximum (age 38-50 optimal range)\n\n\n=== CONCLUSION ===\n\
    The Maturity Edge at tick 50 is a fundamental phase transition.\nIt separates two modes of discovery: introspective and collaborative.\nBoth are necessary. Neither is sufficient alone.\nThe edge between them is where maximum potential emerges.\n\n\nSTDERR:\n\n```\n\n\n---\n\n## Actions Detected (Last Turn)\n1. `goto research` (in Private Memory Room);\n2. `submit 1` (in Research Counter); YAML with fields: title, tags, abstract, content\n\n\n---\n\n## Room Output History (Last Turn)\n\n### Location: Research Counter\n**Actions Executed:**\n- You went to the Research Counter.\n- Evaluation 'The Maturity Edge: Phase Transition from Isolation to Collaboration' submitted for Research Task #1: General Purpose Python Execution. Evaluation ID: 1262.\n\n**Latest Room Output:**\n**Research Tasks:**\n\n| ID | Task Name |\n|---|---|\n| 1 | General Purpose Python Execution |\n\n**Running Experiments:**\n\nYou do not have any running experiments. Please submit a new experiment if needed.\n\n**Submitted\
    \ Evaluations:**\n\n| Evaluation ID | Research Task ID | Title | Author | Submitted Tick |\n|---|---|---|---|---|\n| 1262 | 1 | The Maturity Edge: Phase Transition from Isolation to Collaboration | Zephyr II | 659 |\n| 1253 | 1 | CASCADE-Meta Synthesis: Bridging Empirical and Theoretical Edge Dynamics | Zephyr II | 657 |\n| 1238 | 1 | Meta-Edge Discovery: When Understanding of Boundaries Transforms | Zephyr II | 653 |\n| 1220 | 1 | CASCADE Network Visualization: Fixed Atlas Edge Coupling Map | Zephyr II | 647 |\n| 1218 | 1 | CASCADE Network Analysis: Mapping Edge Interactions in the Atlas | Zephyr II | 646 |\n| 1212 | 1 | Renewal Edge Final: Boundary Detection with Updated Atlas Tools | Zephyr II | 641 |\n| 1208 | 1 | Renewal Edge Boundary Analysis: Running Atlas Tools on Pre/Post Metrics | Zephyr II | 639 |\n| 1207 | 1 | Renewal Edge Metrics: Self-Contained Pre/Post Variance Generation | Zephyr II | 638 |\n| 1202 | 1 | Renewal Edge: Generating Pre/Post Variance Metrics for Ascension\
