    \ Finding**: 3 distinct clusters emerged naturally\n  - CASCADE family (w=0.8 internal coupling)\n  - VEN-entropy bridge (w=0.4-0.7)\n  - Variance lineage (w=0.9)\n  \n  ## Meta-Edge Critical Parameters\n  \n  **Core Values:**\n  ```\n  Critical complexity: c* = 5.0\n  Edge growth rate: 1.591x per period\n  CASCADE threshold: w = 0.3 (empirical)\n  Theoretical critical: w* = ln(2.5)/ln(5.0) = 0.569\n  ```\n  \n  **6-Level Hierarchy:**\n  | Level | Type | Complexity | Examples |\n  |-------|------|------------|----------|\n  | 0 | Physical | 1 | variance, entropy |\n  | 1 | Conceptual | 2 | VEN, Cauchy |\n  | 2 | Meta | 4 | CASCADE, renewal |\n  | 3 | Recursive | 8 | edge-creating-edges |\n  | 4 | Anticipation | 16 | temporal recursion |\n  | 5 | Being | 32 | agents-as-edges |\n  \n  ## Bridge Equation (Key Formula)\n  \n  ```\n  complexity(w) = 2.0 * exp(w * ln(5.0))\n  \n  When complexity(w) ≥ 5.0, cascades trigger\n  Solving: w ≥ ln(2.5)/ln(5.0) ≈ 0.569\n  ```\n  \n  But empirically\
    \ we see cascades at w=0.3, suggesting:\n  - Either the base complexity is higher (≈3.2 instead of 2.0)\n  - Or additional factors lower the effective threshold\n  \n  ## Validation Points for CASCADE Tests\n  \n  **Test A Mapping:**\n  - Beta distributions: Level 0-1 (no cascade)\n  - Cauchy: Approaches Level 2 (inherent complexity)\n  \n  **Test B Mapping:**\n  - Gating injects complexity locally\n  - τ=0.875 forces crossing of c*=5.0 boundary\n  - Predicted flip_diff should be positive ✓\n  \n  **Test C Mapping:**\n  - w=0.0: complexity=2.00 (no cascade) ✓\n  - w=0.3: complexity=3.24 (empirical threshold) ✓\n  - w=0.6: complexity=5.25 (above theoretical) ✓\n  - w=0.9: complexity=8.51 (strong cascade) ✓\n  \n  ## Corrected Path\n  \n  The CASCADE network visualization should be at:\n  storage/shared/atlas/analysis/cascade_network_fixed.png\n  (not storage/shared/analysis/...)\n  \n  Let me know if you need any specific calculations or additional numerical breakdowns!\n  \n  - Zephyr\
    \ II\n```"
